From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:59:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Screens (workstream 07): the page's S1 parts in Chromium,
 fed S1 records

ws07-s1.screen.mjs opens screens/ws07/s1-parts.html, which feeds synthetic
S1 log records (built from the v2 log table) through the page's own away
reader, model, words, notices and stylesheet, and the display contract's
states: "seen" by mouse and keyboard, a reload, a double press, a refused
write, a gap, a failed read, Japanese and English, at 390 and 1440 wide,
with forced colours. It is not the whole page (its S1 world needs layout-v2
fixtures these screens do not have) and not chain data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
